{
  "id": "29505_kinsetsu",
  "headword": "{近接|きんせつ}",
  "reading": "きんせつ",
  "romaji": "kinsetsu",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "proximity; adjacency; coming close",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "proximity; adjacency; coming close",
      "explanation": "Being or coming very near to something in space or time. A formal word used of locations, objects, and dates, and in technical fields such as sensors and photography."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29505_kinsetsu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{二|ふた}つの{街|まち}は{近接|きんせつ}している。",
      "english": "The two towns are close to each other.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29505_kinsetsu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{台風|たいふう}が{本州|ほんしゅう}に{近接|きんせつ}してきた。",
      "english": "The typhoon has drawn close to Honshu.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29505_kinsetsu_ex3",
      "japanese": "{住宅|じゅうたく}{街|がい}に{近接|きんせつ}した{工場|こうじょう}では、{騒音|そうおん}が{問題|もんだい}になりやすい。",
      "english": "At factories close to residential areas, noise tends to become a problem.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Combines {近|きん} (near) + {接|せつ} (touch, adjoin). Being or coming close to something in space or time; a formal alternative to {近|ちか}づく.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ～に{近接|きんせつ}する: to be adjacent to ～\n- {近接|きんせつ}{戦|せん}: close-quarters combat\n- {近接|きんせつ}{撮影|さつえい}: close-up photography\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {隣接|りんせつ}: adjoining — specifically sharing a border, right next to\n- {接近|せっきん}: approach — emphasizes the movement of drawing nearer",
